# Build context exclusions for api/Dockerfile.
#
# THE FIRST ENTRY IS THE IMPORTANT ONE. api/.env exists in every working copy
# and carries live Azure storage-account credentials. A build context that
# includes it puts those keys in a layer of an image published to GHCR, where
# anyone with a pull token can `docker save` and read them back out. The
# Dockerfile also copies three explicit paths rather than `COPY . .`, so this
# file is the second of two independent guards, not the only one.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Never ship an Azure deployment descriptor or the zip it produces.
.azure
.deployment
deploy.zip
codepush-infrastructure.bicep
parameters.json
_makezip.js

# Rebuilt inside the image; a host-built copy would shadow it with whatever
# node version and OS the laptop happened to have.
node_modules
bin

# Local storage backends and their persisted state.
JsonStorage.json
__azurite_db_*
__blobstorage__
__queuestorage__
uploads
downloads

# Certificates. HTTPS is never enabled in the container (Caddy terminates TLS
# one hop upstream), so these have no business in the image even if present.
certs
*.crt
*.pem
*.key
*.cnf

# Dev-only tooling and docs — no effect on the runtime, but they invalidate the
# build cache on every edit.
.eslintrc.json
prettier.config.js
.vscode
*.md
test
